# NorthNarrow COMBAT-state ip6tables ruleset (BUG-031 / block 2).
#
# Loaded by NetworkIsolator::engage() via `ip6tables-restore`, ALONGSIDE
# the v4 ruleset (combat-rules.v4). On COMBAT entry the agent drops the
# host's IPv6 DATA on INPUT, OUTPUT, and FORWARD — but PRESERVES the v6
# stack.
#
# Why this is NOT a mirror of combat-rules.v4: v4 isolation keeps ARP
# alive because ARP is L2, OUTSIDE the filter table. v6 Neighbor
# Discovery (NDP) and Multicast Listener Discovery (MLD) ride ICMPv6 IN
# this table, so a bare catch-all DROP would brick neighbour resolution
# — the host could not even reach the management carve-out gateway over
# v6 (reaching it requires NDP first). We therefore RETURN the essential
# ICMPv6 control plane before the DROP, so isolation drops DATA, not the
# stack — the v6 analogue of v4's ARP staying up at L2.
#
# Owned limit (BUG-031): this leaves an ICMPv6 NDP/MLD control channel
# open on the local segment during isolation (a same-segment attacker
# could in principle tunnel over it; a remote/routed one cannot).
#
# Beta Step 4b carve-out marker (same as v4): engage() replaces the
# `# >>> NORTHNARROW_MGMT_CARVEOUT <<<` line with ip6tables ACCEPT rules
# for each IPv6 CIDR in /etc/northnarrow/combat-allow.cidrs (default-
# empty = no carve-out). Keep the marker immediately before the DROP.
#
# `ip6tables-restore` flushes the v6 filter table by default before
# applying these rules (replacing any prior user rules — same semantics
# as the v4 ruleset; see BUG-041).
*filter
:NORTHNARROW_COMBAT - [0:0]
-A INPUT -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
-A OUTPUT -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
-A FORWARD -j NORTHNARROW_COMBAT
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -i lo -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -o lo -j RETURN
# --- preserve the v6 stack: ICMPv6 control plane (drop DATA, not the stack) ---
# ICMPv6 errors + PMTUD: 1 dest-unreachable, 2 packet-too-big, 3 time-exceeded, 4 parameter-problem
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 1 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 2 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 3 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 4 -j RETURN
# MLD: 130 query, 131 report (v1), 132 done, 143 report (v2) — multicast membership NDP depends on
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 130 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 131 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 132 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 143 -j RETURN
# NDP: 133 router-solicit, 134 router-advert, 135 neighbour-solicit, 136 neighbour-advert, 137 redirect
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 133 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 134 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 135 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 136 -j RETURN
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -p ipv6-icmp --icmpv6-type 137 -j RETURN
# >>> NORTHNARROW_MGMT_CARVEOUT <<<
-A NORTHNARROW_COMBAT -j DROP
COMMIT
